RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
February 19, 2018

The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne convened in a special meeting on this date
beginning at 6:00 p.m. in City Council Chambers for the purpose of collective labor bargaining
with the Cheyenne Professional Fire Fighters, International Association of Fire Fighters, Local
No. 279.  Present were:  MAYOR – Marian J. Orr; COUNCIL MEMBERS – Bryan Cook, Richard
Johnson (arriving at 6:04 p.m.), Mike Luna, Dr. Mark Rinne, Scott Roybal and Dicky Shanor.
Absent:  Rocky Case, Pete Laybourn and Jeff White.  Also present:  Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk;
Sylvia Hackl, City Attorney; Ron Downey, City Treasurer, and Chief Greg Hoggatt, Fire and
Rescue Department.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Mayor Orr advised the meeting would be audio recorded, and stated that Wyoming State
Statute §16-4-405(a)(x) of the Public Meetings Act allows the governing body to meet in executive
session to consider or tender offers regarding salaries, wages or other terms and conditions of
employment during negotiations with the fire fighters union and that any motion approved by the
governing body to move into executive session during the special meetings would be pursuant to
this section of statute.  Mayor Orr advised when the governing body met in executive session, they
would be meeting in the Mayor’s Conference Room, and when the Fire Union requests to meet in
caucus, they may utilize Room 104.

Mayor Orr stated spokespersons for the City during the negotiation process are herself,
City Council President Dr. Mark Rinne and Council Vice-President Rocky Case, and
spokespersons for the Union were Jonathon Bertsch, Union President, and Bill Hinz, Union Vice-
President.  Mayor Orr noted that any collective Labor Agreement that may be reached between the
City and the Union must be approved by the governing body with the agreement placed on a
regular City Council meeting agenda and approved through the Council’s usual procedures.

Mayor Orr stated the governing body has had the opportunity to individually review the
proposed agreement that was submitted at the February 16th special meeting, and suggested the
governing meet in executive session to discuss.   She noted that upon return from executive session,
review of the agreement would begin on a section-by-section basis.  Mr. Bertsch inquired whether
there were any amendments or changes by the City since the February 16th meeting.  Mayor Orr
responded that there was some clean-up language they had noticed that would be proposed.  Dr.
Rinne moved to meet in executive session, seconded by Mr. Cook.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes”
– all members of the governing body present.  For the record, Mayor Orr identified, in addition to
members of the governing body present, the City Clerk, City Attorney, City Treasurer and Chief
of the Fire and Rescue Department would also be present at the executive session.  [City Clerk
note: Audio recording of the special meeting was stopped; executive session convened at 6:09 p.m.
in the Mayor’s Conference Room]

Following closure of the executive session and Union representatives returning to Council
Chambers from caucus, Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at 7:26 p.m.  Representatives
then reviewed the proposed agreement section-by-section, noting mutual agreement on numerous
sections.  Review included: Substantive changes that will differ from current contract provisions,
and clerical changes and clarifications.  Sections requested to be “pulled” for further discussion
included Section 8, Grievance Procedures; Section 21, Classification of Employment and Basic
Wages; Section 31, Health, Dental and Life Insurance; Section 45, Shift Trainers, and Section 47,
Labor/Management Relations.  Mr. Bertsch submitted copies of proposed Union changes to
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
Sections 8, 21 and 45.  It was mutually agreed that existing contract Sections 41, Testing of Aerial
Devices, and 46, Wildland, would be removed from inclusion in the new agreement.  For the
record, Mr. Bertsch stated the Union is comfortable with everything that has been agreed upon,
and presented and discussed proposed Union changes to Sections 8, 21 and 45.  Mayor Orr
discussed proposed City changes to Sections 8, 31 and 47, and advised the City will further review
the Union’s proposed changes as well as those sections that were “pulled” during the section-by-
section review.  Dr. Rinne moved to meet in executive session, seconded by Mr. Cook.  Motion
carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present.  [City Clerk note: Audio
recording of the special meeting was stopped; executive session convened at 8:16 p.m. in the
Mayor’s Conference Room]

Following closure of the executive session, Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at
9:22 p.m.  Mutual agreement was reached on revisions to Sections 8 and 21.  Pursuant to proposed
City changes to Section 31, Mr. Bertsch requested time for the Union to caucus with Mayor Orr
recessing the meeting at 9:28 p.m.  [City Clerk note: Audio recording of the special meeting was
stopped]  Mayor Orr reconvened the meeting at 9:32 p.m.  Mr. Bertsched expressed the Union’s
agreement to the wording change in Section 31, and mutual agreement was reached on changes to
Sections 45 and 47.  Both parties confirmed provisions for the 2018-2019 Collective Labor
Agreement had been reached and negotiations were complete.  Comments were made and
appreciation expressed by City and Union representatives concerning this year’s positive
negotiating process; benefit of the new labor/management meetings that have been held pursuant
to the current contract, and continuing positive communications.
Mayor Orr stated the purpose of the special meeting had been met, and there being no
business previously noted for the special meeting, adjourned the meeting at 9:44 p.m.
/s/ Carol Intlekofer, MMC, City Clerk

This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.
Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle

March 2, 2018
```
